.TH HIRO 1 "August 2026" "HIRO" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hiro \- enroll and manage face templates for HIRO authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hiro
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
HIRO provides Windows Hello-style face authentication on Linux using the
built-in IR camera. \fBhiro\fR talks to the \fBhirod\fR(8) daemon to enroll,
test, and manage encrypted face templates.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B enroll [USER] [--max N]
Capture face templates. Stand in front of the IR camera and follow the
quality feedback; frames that are blurry, too small, static, or duplicates
are rejected automatically.
.TP
.B test
Run a verification attempt against your own templates.
.TP
.B list [USER]
List enrolled templates.
.TP
.B remove USER --id N
Remove one template.
.TP
.B clear [USER]
Remove all templates.
.TP
.B snapshot PATH
Capture one frame to a PGM file (debug aid).
.TP
.B doctor
Run hardware diagnostics: camera discovery, IR detection, emitter support,
model integrity, and daemon reachability.
.TP
.B status
Show daemon status.
.TP
.B ping
Check daemon reachability.
.TP
.B prewarm
Ask the daemon to warm the camera and models.
.TP
.B reload
Reload the daemon configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --socket PATH
Daemon socket path (default \fI/run/hirod/hirod.sock\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hirod (8),
.BR pam_hiro (8),
.BR hiro.conf (5)
